    "explanation": "<p class=\"text-sm leading-6 text-muted-foreground\">Internal energy of a system is the total energy stored by all its particles. This includes both <em>kinetic energy</em> (energy due to particle motion) and <em>potential energy</em> (energy due to forces between particles and their positions). When you heat a substance, you increase its internal energy.</p>",
